'''''Cormoran Strike''''' is a series of [[crime fiction]] novels written by British author [[J. K. Rowling]] under the [[pen name]] Robert Galbraith. The story chronicles the cases of the fictional [[private investigator|private detective]] Cormoran Strike and his business partner Robin Ellacott. Eight novels have so far been published in a planned series of ten.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.jkrowling.com/new-robert-galbraith-book-the-running-grave/ | title=New Robert Galbraith book, The Running Grave | date=2023-04-27 | access-date=2023-04-27 |website=jkrowling.com |language=en}}</ref> The eighth novel, titled ''[[The Hallmarked Man]]'', was released on 2 September 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=The Hallmarked Man by Robert Galbraith |url=https://www.littlebrown.co.uk/titles/robert-galbraith/the-hallmarked-man/9781408723784/ |website=Hachette UK}}</ref> A ninth, titled ''Sleep Tight, Evangeline'' was announced by Rowling on 13 February 2026.<ref name=":0" /> As of February 2024, the series has sold more than 20 million copies worldwide and was published in more than 50 countries, being translated into 43 languages.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Tom Burke and Holliday Grainger return in BBC's Strike – The Ink Black Heart |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2024/tom-burke-holliday-grainger-return-strike-the-ink-black-heart/|date=2024-02-14|access-date=2024-02-19 |website=BBC Media Centre |language=en}}</ref>

The novels are adapted into the television programme ''[[Strike (TV series)|Strike]]'', which began airing on [[BBC One]] in the United Kingdom in August 2017.<ref>{{Cite magazine |title=New details about J.K. Rowling's BBC series revealed |url=https://www.ew.com/article/2015/09/24/jk-rowling-cormoran-strike-bbc-series |first=Kevin P. |last=Sullivan |date=2015-09-24 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |access-date=2015-12-09}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=BBC Orders Adaptation of J.K. Rowling's Third Cormoran Strike novel |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/bbc-orders-adaptation-jk-rowlings-third-cormoran-strike-novel-1039985 |date=2017-09-17 |first=Georg |last=Szalai |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |access-date=2017-09-29}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/m000m82m|title = BBC One – Strike, Lethal White, Episode 1}}</ref>
